<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Florida Parishes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> Parishes are eight parishes of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> lying east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a> and north of Lake Pontchartrain. Formerly part of Spanish West Florida, the area rebelled as the Republic of West Florida in 1810, was annexed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> the same year and joined the state of Louisiana in 1812.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florida-parishes.jpg" alt="Florida Parishes" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: getmahesh · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown_Baton_Rouge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
